{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "26105580",
      "title": "Classes & TypeScript",
      "lectureOrder": 759,
      "videoOrder": 699,
      "sourceHash": "447f3b2c24e74ed707cedc6a91fced3eb7d370dd74dad50bc9cf07e3da2a7309",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.25,
          "end": 4.59,
          "en": "Instructor: Now, I got one last feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.59,
          "end": 6.96,
          "en": "which I also wanna cover here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.96,
          "end": 11.96,
          "en": "And there will be classes and interfaces with TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.39,
          "end": 16.8,
          "en": "And we know classes from modern JavaScript already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.8,
          "end": 19.65,
          "en": "You can define blueprints for objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.65,
          "end": 21.48,
          "en": "with help of the class keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.48,
          "end": 25.26,
          "en": "And again, this is a keyword supported in TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.26,
          "end": 29.22,
          "en": "but it is actually also supported in modern JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.22,
          "end": 31.41,
          "en": "Now with classes, as I just said,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.41,
          "end": 34.59,
          "en": "you can define blueprints for objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.59,
          "end": 37.29,
          "en": "which you plan on instantiating.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.29,
          "end": 41.61,
          "en": "For example, here I could create a person class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.61,
          "end": 44.1,
          "en": "or let's maybe create a student class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.1,
          "end": 48.963,
          "en": "and then you can add properties and methods to that class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.95,
          "end": 51.09,
          "en": "So for example here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.09,
          "end": 53.64,
          "en": "we could say that every student",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.64,
          "end": 56.43,
          "en": "should have a first name property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.43,
          "end": 60.18,
          "en": "and we can assign types to these properties to make it clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.18,
          "end": 64.44,
          "en": "that this first name property here should be a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.44,
          "end": 67.77,
          "en": "And then we maybe also have a last name which is a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.77,
          "end": 70.41,
          "en": "maybe an age which is a number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.41,
          "end": 75.123,
          "en": "and maybe a courses array, which is an array of strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.08,
          "end": 79.023,
          "en": "Now with that we define such a blueprint.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.89,
          "end": 83.03999999999999,
          "en": "Now we can also add a constructor function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.03999999999999,
          "end": 85.98,
          "en": "a constructor method to this class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.98,
          "end": 89.31,
          "en": "to then define the default methods that will be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.31,
          "end": 94.31,
          "en": "when we instantiate a new object based on that class here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.74000000000001,
          "end": 97.77000000000001,
          "en": "And here we could accept certain arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.77000000000001,
          "end": 102.18,
          "en": "like first which is a string, last which is a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 102.18,
          "end": 103.74000000000001,
          "en": "age which is a number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.74000000000001,
          "end": 106.8,
          "en": "and courses which is an array of strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.8,
          "end": 109.68,
          "en": "And you see that I have the same argument names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.68,
          "end": 111.84,
          "en": "as I have properties and therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.84,
          "end": 115.02000000000001,
          "en": "we could then set first name equal to first,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.02000000000001,
          "end": 117.42,
          "en": "this last name equal to last,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.42,
          "end": 122.14,
          "en": "this age equal to age and this courses is equal to courses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 123.81,
          "end": 125.07,
          "en": "like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.07,
          "end": 128.91,
          "en": "And if we do that, we can define a new student down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.91,
          "end": 132.75,
          "en": "by instantiating this student class like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.75,
          "end": 137.04,
          "en": "and then we can pass in these values for our parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.04,
          "end": 139.35,
          "en": "to this constructor function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 139.35,
          "end": 141.45,
          "en": "By the way, of course your class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.45,
          "end": 145.02,
          "en": "doesn't have to take any arguments in the constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 145.02,
          "end": 149.52,
          "en": "You could also set those properties in a different way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.52,
          "end": 152.16,
          "en": "for example, by assigning default values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 152.16,
          "end": 156.09300000000002,
          "en": "or after you created an object with the dot notation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.05,
          "end": 159.81,
          "en": "But here, I'll then pass in my values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.81,
          "end": 161.74,
          "en": "for these different arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 165.18,
          "end": 166.59,
          "en": "like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 166.59,
          "end": 170.1,
          "en": "and with that, we create such a new object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.1,
          "end": 172.98,
          "en": "And on this student we can now use the dot notation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 172.98,
          "end": 175.14,
          "en": "to access the different properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 175.14,
          "end": 179.01,
          "en": "and if we had any methods besides the constructor function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 179.01,
          "end": 181.83,
          "en": "we could call those methods as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 181.83,
          "end": 184.77,
          "en": "And speaking of that, we can add a method here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 184.77,
          "end": 186.78,
          "en": "Let's say the enroll method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 186.78,
          "end": 191.31,
          "en": "which allows us to enroll this student into a new course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 191.31,
          "end": 194.07,
          "en": "and therefore we could accept the course name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 194.07,
          "end": 198.99,
          "en": "as a argument here and then add it to courses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 198.99,
          "end": 200.19,
          "en": "like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 200.19,
          "end": 204.21,
          "en": "And that's how you add a method to such a class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 204.21,
          "end": 207.9,
          "en": "This is the method shorthand notation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.9,
          "end": 209.88,
          "en": "You have the method name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 209.88,
          "end": 213.54,
          "en": "then your parameter list and then the function body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 213.54,
          "end": 217.77,
          "en": "so it's basically defined like a regular JavaScript function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 217.77,
          "end": 219.72,
          "en": "with the important difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 219.72,
          "end": 222.27,
          "en": "that we don't have the function keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 222.27,
          "end": 224.01,
          "en": "We don't have that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 224.01,
          "end": 226.41,
          "en": "That then is how we add a method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.41,
          "end": 228.84,
          "en": "And now we could call this method here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 228.84,
          "end": 233.37,
          "en": "and call enroll and pass in React as another course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 233.37,
          "end": 235.17000000000002,
          "en": "this student is enrolled in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 235.17000000000002,
          "end": 238.86,
          "en": "and thereafter, if you would access student.courses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 238.86,
          "end": 243.573,
          "en": "this would include both Angular and React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 245.22,
          "end": 247.74,
          "en": "That's how we can define a class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 247.74,
          "end": 251.22,
          "en": "Now the special thing about TypeScript and classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 251.22,
          "end": 254.28,
          "en": "is that we can define all the properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 254.28,
          "end": 256.53,
          "en": "this class will have in advance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 256.53,
          "end": 259.98,
          "en": "and set the types for these different properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 259.98,
          "end": 263.55,
          "en": "In standard JavaScript, we would not do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 263.55,
          "end": 266.34,
          "en": "we would not have these property assignments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 266.34,
          "end": 268.74,
          "en": "Instead, properties would be added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 268.74,
          "end": 271.59,
          "en": "by just setting them inside of the constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 271.59,
          "end": 272.52,
          "en": "With TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 272.52,
          "end": 276.48,
          "en": "you can define them ahead of time including their types,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 276.48,
          "end": 279.99,
          "en": "and also very important, with TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 279.99,
          "end": 283.95,
          "en": "you can control whether a property or a method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 283.95,
          "end": 288.95,
          "en": "should be publicly accessible or if it should be private.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 289.05,
          "end": 292.5,
          "en": "Now, private properties and methods can only be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 292.5,
          "end": 296.46,
          "en": "from inside this class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 296.46,
          "end": 300.93,
          "en": "Public methods and properties can be accessed from outside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 300.93,
          "end": 303.39,
          "en": "through this dot notation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 303.39,
          "end": 305.04,
          "en": "And therefore, as you can tell,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 305.04,
          "end": 309.03,
          "en": "by default all these properties and methods are public",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 309.03,
          "end": 311.853,
          "en": "because by default I can access them all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 312.84,
          "end": 316.89,
          "en": "But we could say that courses should be private",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 316.89,
          "end": 319.23,
          "en": "by adding the private keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 319.23,
          "end": 321.603,
          "en": "in front of this property definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 322.62,
          "end": 325.08,
          "en": "And then we could of course add another method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 325.08,
          "end": 327.48,
          "en": "let's say list courses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 327.48,
          "end": 331.74,
          "en": "and there we then return this.courses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 331.74,
          "end": 333.57,
          "en": "Now this might be a bit redundant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 333.57,
          "end": 336.69,
          "en": "we don't really gain a lot by doing it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 336.69,
          "end": 339.33,
          "en": "We gain a bit more if we call slice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 339.33,
          "end": 342.39,
          "en": "because then at least we return a copy of courses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 342.39,
          "end": 346.17,
          "en": "and make sure that if someone would push a new element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 346.17,
          "end": 348.96,
          "en": "onto this array from outside of this class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 348.96,
          "end": 353.01,
          "en": "the original array inside of the class would not be altered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 353.01,
          "end": 355.743,
          "en": "but in general, this is just an example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 356.88,
          "end": 359.31,
          "en": "Now with those adjustments made,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 359.31,
          "end": 363.87,
          "en": "I can't access student.courses here, I get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 363.87,
          "end": 365.94,
          "en": "Instead, I can call list courses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 365.94,
          "end": 370.53,
          "en": "if I wanna see all the courses this student is enrolled in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 370.53,
          "end": 374.58,
          "en": "And that stands simply another TypeScript feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 374.58,
          "end": 378.45,
          "en": "which you will also see in action throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 378.45,
          "end": 380.34,
          "en": "Now, it's also worth pointing out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 380.34,
          "end": 383.58,
          "en": "that it's a very common pattern in TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 383.58,
          "end": 386.7,
          "en": "that you define properties like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 386.7,
          "end": 390.42,
          "en": "and you then assign values to those properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 390.42,
          "end": 391.95,
          "en": "through the constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 391.95,
          "end": 395.67,
          "en": "You don't necessarily do it in all the classes you create,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 395.67,
          "end": 397.32,
          "en": "especially with Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 397.32,
          "end": 399.84000000000003,
          "en": "You will see a lot of classes where you don't do it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 399.84000000000003,
          "end": 403.02,
          "en": "but it's definitely all the not uncommon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 403.02,
          "end": 406.08,
          "en": "And because it's so common to assign values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 406.08,
          "end": 408.75,
          "en": "to those properties which you defined before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 408.75,
          "end": 411.87,
          "en": "you can do it in one step with TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 411.87,
          "end": 414.63,
          "en": "Instead of defining your properties here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 414.63,
          "end": 419.01,
          "en": "you can add these modifier, these accessor keywords",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 419.01,
          "end": 422.82,
          "en": "in front of your parameters in the constructor method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 422.82,
          "end": 426.3,
          "en": "and add public in front of all the parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 426.3,
          "end": 429.58,
          "en": "that should be set up as public properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 430.44,
          "end": 433.26,
          "en": "and add private in front of all the parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 433.26,
          "end": 436.83,
          "en": "that should be set up as private properties.",
